      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a2d93e99",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: suspect_is_a_male_wearing_clothing; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a police officer in uniform, with text that humorously suggests the suspect 'kinda looks like a mountain panda' but the creator doesn't want to 'assume'. This is a racially charged and harmful stereotype, as it uses the visual appearance of a person (likely a Black man, given the context of 'mountain panda' as a derogatory term) to imply criminality or other negative traits based on physical resemblance to an animal. The meme relies on a harmful racial stereotype that equates Black men with animals, which is a form of anti-Black racism. The intent is to mock or dehumanize a group based on appearance, which can perpetuate prejudice and reinforce harmful societal attitudes. The juxtaposition of the serious police scene with the absurd, racially charged comparison is intended to elicit laughter at the expense of a marginalized group, making it a harmful meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f2810cad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
